 "result": "I updated `package.json`, added `README.md`, and added `src/server.ts` so `npm run daemon` has something to start. I haven't run any of it, and nothing is installed.\n\n- **Scripts:** `test:unit`, `typecheck`, `daemon` and `healthcheck` were already in `package.json`. I didn't add any, but I changed `daemon` to run `src/server.ts` with `TEST_DAEMON_PORT=8089`.\n- **Why the change:** the old `daemon` script ran `auth.ts`, which never calls `listen()`, so the daemon would have exited immediately.\n- **`src/server.ts` (new):** listens on `DAEMON_PORT` and routes `/status`, `/v2/auth`, `POST /v2/upload` and `/v2/billing/export`. Anything else gets a 404. It does not serve `/v2/billing`, `/v2/billing/invoices` or `/v2/storage/history`, which the React components still call.\n- **`README.md` (new):** it has a \"Running unit tests\" section (`npm run test:unit`, with a note that there is no `npm test`). A second section covers starting the daemon, with the port 8089, the 8000ms timeout, `scratch/`, and the cleanup script.",
